{
  "$description": "The ColdLight MATRIX (docs/design/coldlight-matrix.md). A THEME is a COORDINATE in this matrix, not a hand-authored bundle. Four facets: ANCESTOR (Personality, owns font) x STRUCTURE (Space, owns radius + edge.width) x MATERIAL (Matter, owns fill, ink, edge.color) x ATMOSPHERE (Energy, owns shadows, back_glow, tints, anim). GENERATED into Rust by build.rs; never hand-edited downstream.",
  "$laws": [
    "M1 - ONE value per facet, exactly. The untyped `stack: &[&str]` and the two-contradictory-bases bug are gone by construction.",
    "M2 - An ancestor ALONE is a complete look. Its `native` fills every facet, so a facet value need only declare the axes it changes; everything else falls back to the ancestor's natives. This is the same override/additive rule compose() already uses, one tier up.",
    "M3 - Legality is DATA. Every facet value appears in exactly one of native/allowed/forbidden for EVERY ancestor. A value left unclassified fails the build - that is what stops the matrix rotting as values are added.",
    "M4 - edge is SPLIT: width is geometry (STRUCTURE), colour is substance (MATERIAL). Without this an atmosphere has to reach outside its lane to recolour an edge, which is the exact defect the matrix exists to close.",
    "M5 - Typography belongs to the ANCESTOR and is never a free knob. It is the most identity-carrying choice a movement makes."
  ],
